Abstract
Abstract
With the continuous growth of China's economy and urbanisation, the number of
motor vehicles has increased tremendously, and the original urban road transport
planning is no longer able to meet the increasing travel needs of people. The full
exploitation of urban underground space resources and the development of
underground transportation is an important way to solve urban traffic congestion.
Shield tunnel construction has also become a mainstream technology and
development direction.
As China's experience in shield construction continues to accumulate, more and
more large diameter shield projects are being implemented. Although shield
construction is relatively mature and has obvious advantages, there are still a lot of
uncertainties in the construction process and shield construction accidents do occur
from time to time. It is important to pay attention to safety risk management in shield
construction, carry out safety risk identification and evaluation studies, and
effectively reduce the level of safety risks during construction by implementing
risk-based decision-making, so as to minimise casualties and economic losses caused
by risks. Therefore, it is necessary and urgent to conduct safety risk studies on the
construction of oversized diameter shields.
In this paper, the construction of a shield section tunnel for a new expressway
project in Shanghai is used as the research object to carry out a study on the safety
risks of oversized shield construction. A 15.56m diameter, 123m long, mud-water
balanced shield was used for the tunnel construction, which is currently the largest
shield in Shanghai and has implications for future risk management studies of similar
shield construction. The specific research includes the following aspects.
(1) Applying the WBS-RBS method and the expert survey method to identify
risks, the shield construction was divided into five main construction stages:
"pre-construction preparation, starting and receiving work well construction, shield


